      "id": 482183,
      "username": "madhusona",
      "name": "Madusudhanan Bairappan",
      "created_at": "2025-09-26T07:27:55.926Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Vinay1\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"154373\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/v/898d66/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Vinay1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>and i gave the role for a user, the user also has employee role. when i logged-in using the role i am able to change all the fields.so why is that am i missed something or did something wrong?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<h2><a name=\"p-482183-example-setup-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482183-example-setup-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Example Setup</h2>\n<h3><a name=\"p-482183-role-1-read-only-role-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482183-role-1-read-only-role-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Role 1 (Read-only role)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Level 0</strong> → <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Read (no Write)</li>\n<li><strong>Level 1</strong> → <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Read (no Write)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/backhand_index_pointing_right.png?v=15\" title=\":backhand_index_pointing_right:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":backhand_index_pointing_right:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> This means Role 1 can only <em>view</em> all fields.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-482183-role-2-limited-write-role-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482183-role-2-limited-write-role-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Role 2 (Limited write role)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Level 0</strong> → <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Read + Write</li>\n<li><strong>Level 1</strong> → <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Read</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/backhand_index_pointing_right.png?v=15\" title=\":backhand_index_pointing_right:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":backhand_index_pointing_right:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> This means Role 2 can edit fields at <strong>Level 0</strong>, but fields marked as <strong>Level 1</strong> are read-only.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><a name=\"p-482183-result-for-a-user-who-has-both-role-1-role-2-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482183-result-for-a-user-who-has-both-role-1-role-2-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/small_blue_diamond.png?v=15\" title=\":small_blue_diamond:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":small_blue_diamond:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Result for a User who has <em>both</em> Role 1 + Role 2</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>At <strong>Level 0</strong> → since Role 2 has Write, the user can <strong>edit fields</strong> (Role 1’s read-only does not block).</li>\n<li>At <strong>Level 1</strong> → only Read is given, so the user <strong>cannot edit</strong> those fields.</li>\n</ul>",
